 \in [0.005,3]$ au, $\gamma \in [-11,4]$"}]},"validation":{"value":"Autocorrelation length for convergence; Lupus results compared with Andrews2018a","evidence":[{"loc":"4 Modeling Method","quote":"We use the autocorrelation length as a guide to understand at what point in the chain convergence occurs."}]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Derive effective radii and resolved/unresolved status","method":{"value":"R68 and R90 from cumulative flux for 5000 random models from second half of chain; median and 16/84 quantiles; compare reduced chi2 of Nuker vs point source; 84th percentile as upper limit if unresolved","evidence":[{"loc":"4 Modeling Method","quote":"We randomly sample 5000 models from the second half of our MCMC chain, and for each model we calculate $R_{\text{eff}}$ ."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Compared with Andrews2018a Lupus sizes; stuck-walker test","evidence":[{"loc":"4 Modeling Method","quote":"our method retrieves the same disk sizes as those in (cite: Andrews2018a) for most sources"}]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Sample selection","method":{"value":"Remove multiples with separation <=2"; remove 15 spurious models with size uncertainty >66% of size inspected by eye","evidence":[{"loc":"10 Determination and removal of spurious modeling","quote":"Of the 23 disks that meet this metric, we find 15 that are obviously problematic, and hence removed them from our analysis"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":5,"goal":"Derive stellar masses","method":{"value":"Bayesian inference with literature Teff and L (rescaled to Gaia DR2)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2.1 Stellar masses","quote":"we assume an uncertainty of 0.02 dex in the stellar temperature for spectral types earlier than M3 and 0.01 dex for later spectral types and a 0.1 dex uncertainty on all stellar luminosities."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":6,"goal":"Statistical comparison of regions and relations","method":{"value":"Kaplan-Meier CDFs, Anderson-Darling tests, Shapiro-Wilk, Pearson/Spearman, linmix regression of log Reff vs Lmm, M*, L*","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.1 Disk radii and millimeter luminosities","quote":"For this task we use the Bayesian method of linear regression described in (cite: Kelly2007) (as implemented in the `linmix` code by Joshua E. Meyers)"}]},"software":["linmix","lifelines","scipy"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"p<0.05 threshold","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1 Relations between stellar and disk properties","quote":"In cases where the p-value for the chosen statistic is $<0.05$ we consider the data to be correlated."}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"linmix Bayesian regression accounting for errors and upper limits","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Comparison of Lupus linmix fits with Andrews2018a","evidence":[{"loc":"8.1 Lupus comparison","quote":"Our fitting of both the (cite: Andrews2018a) sample and our sample gives results that are consistent with each other"}]}}],"software":[{"name":"CASA","version":"4.7.2-el6; 5.1.1-5.el7","used_for":{"value":"Calibration scripts and averaging","evidence":[{"loc":"3 ALMA Observations and Data Reduction","quote":"For these steps, we use `CASA` version `4.7.2-el6`."}]}},{"name":"GALARIO","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Fourier transform of model images to visibilities","evidence":[{"loc":"4 Modeling Method","quote":"which is Fourier transformed and sampled at the same spatial frequencies as our observational data using `GALARIO` (cite: Tazzari2018)"}]}},{"name":"emcee","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"MCMC fitting","evidence":[{"loc":"4 Modeling Method","quote":"using the `emcee` implementation (cite: Foreman-Mackey2013) of the Markov Chain Monte Carlo method (MCMC)"}]}},{"name":"linmix","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Bayesian linear regression","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.1 Disk radii and millimeter luminosities","quote":"(as implemented in the `linmix` code by Joshua E. Meyers)"}]}},{"name":"lifelines","version":"v0.21.3","used_for":{"value":"Kaplan-Meier estimator","evidence":[{"loc":"footnote 4","quote":"We use the Python lifelines (cite: cameron_davidson_pilon_2019_3240536) Kaplan-Meier implementation."}]}},{"name":"uvplot","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Listed in software section (uv plotting)","evidence":[{"loc":"Software","quote":"uvplot (cite: Tazzariuvplot)"}]}}],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"Disks with estimated sizes","value":"152 (50 Lupus, 58 Cha I, 44 USco)","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"disks","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"4.1 Subsample","quote":"This leaves us with 152 disks: 50 from Lupus, 58 from Cha I and 44 from USco which we include in our analysis."}]},{"quantity":"Median R68 Lupus","value":"46.6","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"5 Results","quote":"Lupus & 30 & 46.6 & 128.1 & 63.2 & 213.1"}]},{"quantity":"Median R68 Cha I","value":"33.9","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"5 Results","quote":"Cha I & 33 & 33.9 & 140.9 & 43.1 & 231.3"}]},{"quantity":"Median R68 USco","value":"26.8","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"5 Results","quote":"USco & 22 & 26.8 & 100.8 & 33.4 & 126.2"}]},{"quantity":"Anderson-Darling significance USco vs Lupus","value":"0.013","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"dimensionless","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"5 Results","quote":"USco & Lupus & 3.4 & $0.013$"}]},{"quantity":"log Reff-log Lmm slope beta, Lupus","value":"0.57","uncertainty":"+/-0.10","units":"dimensionless","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"Table 5.1.1","quote":"$2.20^{+0.14}_{-0.13}$ & $0.57^{+0.10}_{-0.10}$"}]},{"quantity":"log Reff-log Lmm slope beta, Cha I","value":"0.40","uncertainty":"+/-0.06","units":"dimensionless","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"Table 5.1.1","quote":"$1.97^{+0.08}_{-0.08}$ & $0.40^{+0.06}_{-0.06}$"}]},{"quantity":"log Reff-log Lmm slope beta, USco","value":"0.22","uncertainty":"+0.11/-0.10","units":"dimensionless","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"Table 5.1.1","quantity":"","quote":"$1.68^{+0.23}_{-0.22}$ & $0.22^{+0.11}_{-0.10}$"}]},{"quantity":"Temperature index q","value":"0.32 (Cha I); -0.85 (USco)","uncertainty":"+0.33/-0.4 (Cha I); +1.42/-3.1 (USco)","units":"dimensionless","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"6.3 Disk size scaling relations","quote":"values of $q$ of $0.32^{+0.33}_{-0.4}$ for Cha I and $-0.85^{+1.42}_{-3.1}$ for USco"}]},{"quantity":"R90 for near-solar-mass stars","value":"20-103","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"7 Summary","quote":"$R_{\text{90}}$ disk sizes range from 20-103 au."}]},{"quantity":"R90 vs R68 relation","value":"log R90 = -0.037 + 1.1 log R68","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"12 Correlation of R90 and R68","quote":"\log{\ensuremath{
