} \text{(au)}"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"Cha I disks are not smaller than Lupus disks, contrary to Eisner2018","evidence":[{"loc":"7 Summary","quote":"We find that the disks in Cha I are not smaller than those in Lupus as previously suggested in (cite: Eisner2018)"}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"Is the Reff-Lmm relation universal across regions?","experiment":"linmix fits per region for 5 regions","result":"slopes 0.57 (Lupus), 0.40 (Cha I), 0.22 (USco)","finding":"The relation flattens in older regions and is not universal","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"but show for the first time that the relationship is not universal between regions."}]},{"hypothesis":"Are USco disks smaller than those in younger regions?","experiment":"Compare R68 distributions with Anderson-Darling","result":"Median 26.8 au vs 46.6 (Lupus) and 33.9 (Cha I); sig. 0.013-0.014","finding":"USco disks are smaller, though by less than factor 3","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"7 Summary","quote":"USco disk sizes are not drawn from the same distribution of disk sizes as Lupus and Cha I."}]},{"hypothesis":"Are Cha I disks smaller than those in other regions of similar age?","experiment":"Compare homogeneous Cha I and Lupus sizes","result":"Anderson-Darling sig 0.105","finding":"Cha I not smaller than Lupus","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"We find that disks in the 2-3 Myr-old Cha I are not smaller than disks in other regions of similar age"}]},{"hypothesis":"Is the Solar System's outer edge consistent with disk sizes?","experiment":"Compare R90 of Lupus/Cha I disks to ~45 au Kuiper Belt edge","result":"R90 for near-solar-mass stars 20-103 au","finding":"Solar System not an outlier; no truncation required","support":"partially","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"the outer edge of the Solar System, as defined by the Kuiper Belt, is consistent with a population of dust disk sizes which have not experienced significant truncation."}]}],"reasoning":[{"field":"why_this_method","value":"Same modeling as Tripathi2017 and Andrews2018a to get homogeneous sizes","evidence":[{"loc":"1 Introduction","quote":"using the same modeling techniques in order to present a homogeneously derived census of disk sizes within five regions of varying ages"}]}],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Oph and Tau/Aur SMA samples are flux-limited and biased bright","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Oph and Tau/Aur","quote":"the Oph and Tau/Aur samples come from flux-limited SMA observations, and consequently are biased towards brighter objects"}]},{"value":"Correlation tests do not include upper limits and uncertainties","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1 Relations","quote":"A limitation of all these statistical tests is that they do not include upper-limits and uncertainties in the assessment."}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["Age ordering of regions is uncertain with overlapping ages","Unresolved disks at ~0.3-0.7" resolution limit small-size conclusions","Stuck walkers left in chains","Solar System comparison relies on strong assumptions"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"Archival ALMA data from public projects (one set provided by PI)","evidence":[{"loc":"3 ALMA Observations and Data Reduction","quote":"the raw data is taken from the ALMA archive"}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["Per-source averaging parameters","Exact sampler convergence settings per source","Full fit outputs only in electronic version","Andrews2018a Lmm and R68 tables for Oph/Tau/Aur"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"~100s of GB raw for ~180 band 7 datasets; far less after averaging (~ tens of GB)","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"Methods, priors, sampler and software are given and data public, but per-source averaging and several inherited choices are unstated and fits are heavy.","rediscovery_candidate":false,"rediscovery_reason":"Recipe is mostly stated but needs literature inputs and unstated per-source choices; large MCMC runs for ~150 disks.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: Tripathi2017)","why":"Nuker-profile visibility fitting and Reff definition"},{"citation":"(cite: Andrews2018a)","why":"Lupus/Oph/Tau-Aur sizes and Lmm definition, comparison"},{"citation":"(cite: Tazzari2018)","why":"GALARIO"},{"citation":"(cite: Kelly2007)","why":"linmix regression"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: Pascucci2016)","why":"Cha I ALMA survey and stellar mass method"},{"citation":"(cite: Ansdell2016)","why":"Lupus ALMA survey"},{"citation":"(cite: Barenfeld2016)","why":"USco ALMA survey"},{"citation":"(cite: Long2018)","why":"Cha I high-resolution detections"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":["ALMA Lupus survey","ALMA Cha I survey","ALMA USco survey"]}
